# Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** July 2026  
**Last updated:** September 2026

This Privacy Policy describes how **IO HELPER**, a Chrome Manifest V3 browser extension for CYBERSHOKE moderators, handles information.

IO HELPER is developed for use on the official CYBERSHOKE moderation website (`cybershoke.net` and `cybershoke.ru`). It is not a general-purpose browsing tool.

## Summary

IO HELPER does not collect, store on remote servers, sell, rent, or share personal information about users of the extension. Processing that the extension performs to assist moderation happens locally in the user’s browser, except for the limited network requests listed below.

## Information we do not collect

The extension does not collect, transmit, or retain:

- names, email addresses, or account credentials;
- passwords;
- cookies belonging to other sites;
- browsing history outside the CYBERSHOKE moderation pages where the extension runs;
- financial or payment data;
- precise location data;
- advertising, analytics, or telemetry identifiers.

## Local processing

On CYBERSHOKE moderation pages, the extension reads information that is already visible in the page (for example chat history, ticket fields, and server links) in order to:

- analyze chat history and suggest moderation outcomes;
- highlight complaint triggers, duplicate servers, and new accounts;
- translate non-Russian chat messages when that feature is enabled;
- display moderator and offender context (VIP status, Steam account creation date, Faceit ELO);
- fill moderation templates and punishment form fields;
- auto-connect to a game server when the corresponding setting is enabled.

This processing runs on the user’s device.

## Local storage

IO HELPER stores only extension settings and cached configuration in the browser’s extension storage (`chrome.storage.local`), for example:

- feature toggles and user preferences;
- cached moderation configuration fetched from this project’s GitHub repository;
- cached moderator list data used by schedule scanning and server highlighting.

This data remains in the browser profile unless the user clears extension data or uninstalls the extension.

## Network requests

The extension may make requests to:

- the official CYBERSHOKE moderation website (`*.cybershoke.net`, `*.cybershoke.ru`), including the user-data API used by offender tracking;
- this project’s GitHub repository, to download the latest `config.json`;
- FastMM (`mobile.fastmm.win`), to look up public Steam profile metadata (account creation date and Faceit ELO) when those features are enabled;
- Google Translate (`translate.googleapis.com`) and MyMemory (`api.mymemory.translated.net`), when the chat translation feature is enabled.

These requests exist only to support the features above. The extension does not send browsing history or unrelated personal data to these endpoints.

## Third-party services

If translation is enabled, message text is sent to the selected translation provider to obtain a translation. FastMM is queried only with the Steam identifier already present on the moderation page, when Steam/Faceit profile features are enabled.

IO HELPER does not sell, rent, or otherwise share user data with third parties for advertising or analytics.

## Permissions

The extension requests the `storage` permission to save settings locally, and host permissions only for the sites and APIs listed in the extension manifest.

## Changes

This Privacy Policy may be updated when the extension’s features or network endpoints change. The updated text will be published in this repository.

## Contact

Questions about this Privacy Policy can be opened as an issue in the project’s GitHub repository: [https://github.com/K4NT1K/IoHelper](https://github.com/K4NT1K/IoHelper).
